  "guidance": [
    "Companion to workshop-native-regions.json; source boards are artifacts/native-sources/<PROFILE>-board.png. No native image data is embedded here.",
    "layer identifies which original source layer contains a region. Table/stove base regions should exclude the common floor; decor regions need alpha/semantic masks.",
    "Rectangles overlap due to perspective occlusion. Partition visible pixels with explicit foreground priority, and remove large-object pixels from flat table-detail masks. List order is descriptive, not an automatic paint order.",
    "A physical object often needs an inferred clean back or side even when partly occluded in the source. Do not copy the complete front perspective sprite onto every surface.",
    "Optional texturePatches are small material-only source rectangles for the same layer. Verify opacity and colour in the source before using; they are not additional geometry or complete top projections.",
    "Primitive box denotes a solid that may need faceting, rounded edges or an open rim; it does not authorize filling a merged cluster's bounding rectangle.",
    "Primitive rack denotes explicit connected beams, posts, bars, shafts or frame components. Keep negative space open. Distinct components that share a machine must join in world space.",
    "Native tiny tools, jewellery, meat, fish and food are accepted flat on real raised surfaces. Hanging meat and other hanging details are thin vertical cutouts; larger machines, containers, frames and large gems need coherent volume.",
    "Siege and Kennel use 160x192 mosaics. All other profiles in this file use 96x128. Preserve these coordinates rather than rescaling the 5x5 source to 3x3.",
    "Decorative top row is structural height above the footprint, not an extra floor row. Infer object floor/table contact from its native bottom and the support below it."
  ],
